            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jan Mowbray"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good, though I ended up adding half a tsp of sugar just to take off the tart edge. I put the fruit in ziplock baggies in individual servings in the freezer so it's ready when I am - just add juice. I need no ice this way and my immersion blender makes short work of it.",
            "datePublished": "2018-04-14T16:58:01.463Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Elaine"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So delicious, had to make 2 batches because my kids drank it all. I didn't make much of a change. I didn't have ice cubes, so used a cup of frozen strawberries instead, no ice cubes needed. I also used 1 cup of orange juice, threw in one peeled orange and put a couple of spoons of flax seeds to make the smoothie a little more filling. Very, very delicious, will definitely make again and again.",
            "datePublished": "2017-03-26T16:39:16.003Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bobgssc"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is good. I ALWAYS use orange juice that is \"not from concentrate\". Also, I add 1 cup spinach or kale, and 1/4 cup almonds or pecans to make this smoothie cover my basic needs.",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-23T11:39:42.040Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HealthHappy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "There must be a thousand ways to make this fruit smoothie, but this was very good and, of course, I too had to alter the recipe a little. I used a whole orange rather than juice, 1/2 cup unsweetened almond milk, 1/4 cup pomegranate juice, frozen strawberries, 1/2 frozen banana and a T ground flaxseed. It made a 20 oz. smoothie. I would have shared it with my husband if he was here, but since he's not, it's mine, all mine! Delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2014-12-06T13:08:01.533Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sonia Escobar"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is the recipe that came with my blender and it is by far the best one I've tried. However, mine calls for 8 oz. vanilla yogurt and a tablespoon of honey.",
            "datePublished": "2015-09-21T16:54:24.157Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tarah Frost"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummy! I added a few more strawberries, used a frozen banana and omitted the ice cubes. Plus, I used organic, whole orange juice (not from concentrate, which typically has added sugar). It was only slightly sweet, not tart; the perfect accompaniment to lightly savory sandwiches. And a great way to get in lots of healthy fruit!",
            "datePublished": "2011-02-14T20:32:26.617Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Im_Cookn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My family LOVES this smoothie. I've made a couple of tweaks to the recipe, though. Instead of adding ice cubes, I just freeze my strawberries and bananas and add those to the recipe. I also add organic vanilla yogurt to it. Those small tweaks make it thicker and sweeter. YUMMY, YUMMY, YUMMY!!",
            "datePublished": "2012-10-26T15:03:21.493Z"
          },
          {
